  "finding": "Over 22 eligible pools, quoting gross moves the published net fee rate further than display rounding does: the median absolute gross gap is 1.2678 percentage points against a median absolute rounding gap of 0.000904, and the gross gap is the larger of the two on 22 of 22 pools. The largest rounding gap on any pool here is 0.082977 percentage points; the largest gross gap is 101.7989. Read as a share of the rate itself, quoting gross overstates by a median of 49.3% over 22 pools with a non-zero net rate, where rounding moves it by a median of 0.0554%. So the effect v1's narrative led with is the smaller one by three orders of magnitude, and the one it mentioned in passing is the one a reader should worry about. That is the finding the pre-registration committed to publishing either way, and the falsifier's first limb survives: the rounding gap is not zero on every pool, it is simply very small.",
  "finished_at": "2026-08-11T06:33:28+00:00",
